  "step_3": "The decision reason relies on assessing which lottery is more left-skewed—i.e., assigns higher probability to relatively favorable outcomes. As established, Lottery B is more left-skewed (80% chance of no loss vs 75% in A), so the reason would prefer B. However, the individual chooses A based on the smaller loss amount, prioritizing loss magnitude over the higher probability of avoiding loss in B. The individual does consider the probabilities and outcomes but uses a different rule: minimizing the maximum possible loss or focusing on worst-case severity. There is no mention of distributional shape, concentration of probability on better outcomes, or skewness. The justification is outcome-averse (avoid large losses) rather than distribution-averse (favor skewed distributions). Therefore, the reasoning does not align with the skewness-based rule. The information used overlaps partially (probabilities and outcomes), but the integration rule differs fundamentally.",
